# Build context exclusions for Dockerfile.deb / Dockerfile.gui.
#
# Dockerfile.deb does `COPY . /app/`. Without this file the context is ~1.4 GB
# (.venv 562M, dist 486M, release_assets 295M) and every build re-uploads it.
#
# Patterns are deliberately precise. A first attempt used `build_*/` which also
# matched `build_production.py`, and the .deb build then failed with
# "can't open file '/app/build_production.py'". Directory patterns are written
# with explicit names, never globs that can catch a source file.

# --- Virtual environments (host-specific, wrong ABI for the container) ---
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Build output and published artifacts ---
dist/
build/
release_assets/
release_build/
winzip/
linuxzip/
*.exe
*.zip
*.deb
*.AppImage
*.whl

# --- The other OS trees: the container builds the Linux payload from root ---
Linux/
Mac/

# --- Caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[co]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- VCS and editor state ---
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Local scratch that must never influence a build ---
logs/
frozen_*.txt
*.log
benchmark_results.csv
